abstract: >-
  DL_bathy is an open-source two-step pipeline for training a deep learning
  model (DeepLabV3+ with a configurable backbone) to estimate shallow-water
  bathymetry from Sentinel-2 multispectral imagery, using bathymetric
  measurements (e.g. airborne LiDAR) as ground truth. Step 1 prepares,
  aligns, splits, balances, and augments training patches from Sentinel-2
  scenes and reference depth data; Step 2 trains the model, evaluates it on
  a held-out test set, and produces per-patch and aggregate accuracy
  metrics.
